This PR fixes two critical issues preventing the contact form and WhatsApp ordering functionality from working properly, especially on mobile devices.

## Issues Fixed

### 1. Contact Form Not Working
The contact form was completely broken due to an ID mismatch between the HTML and JavaScript:
- **HTML**: `<form id="formulario-contacto">`
- **JavaScript**: `document.getElementById('formContacto')`

This prevented the EmailJS event handler from being attached, so form submissions would fail silently.

**Fix**: Updated the JavaScript selector to match the correct HTML ID:
```javascript
// Before
const formContacto = document.getElementById('formContacto');

// After  
const formContacto = document.getElementById('formulario-contacto');
```

### 2. WhatsApp Button Not Working on Mobile
The WhatsApp ordering button used `type="submit"` and relied on form submission events, which can be unreliable on mobile devices. Additionally, the WhatsApp URL opening strategy wasn't optimized for mobile compatibility.

**Fix**: Changed the button to `type="button"` and moved the logic to a click event handler:
```html
<!-- Before -->
<button type="submit" class="boton-confirmar-envio">

<!-- After -->
<button type="button" class="boton-confirmar-envio" id="btn-enviar-whatsapp">
```

Enhanced the WhatsApp URL opening with a mobile-friendly fallback strategy:
```javascript
try {
  // Try opening in new window first (desktop)
  const nuevaPestaña = window.open(urlWhatsApp, '_blank');
  if (!nuevaPestaña) {
    // Fallback to window.location.href (better for mobile)
    window.location.href = urlWhatsApp;
  }
} catch (error) {
  // Final fallback for mobile devices
  window.location.href = urlWhatsApp;
}
```

## Testing Results
Both fixes have been tested and verified to work correctly:

![Test Results](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7a032b88-fc4f-4896-bc1b-92389c5a4976)

- ✅ Contact form now properly connects to EmailJS and shows success/error messages
- ✅ WhatsApp button works reliably on both desktop and mobile devices
- ✅ All existing functionality preserved (cart clearing, form validation, etc.)
- ✅ Form reset and error handling continue to work as expected

## Impact
These minimal, surgical changes restore core website functionality without affecting any other features. Users can now successfully:
- Send contact messages through the website
- Complete purchases and send orders via WhatsApp on all devices, especially mobile

The fixes maintain the existing user experience while ensuring reliable cross-platform compatibility.

